/// THE REPEATED-GROUP ROW SHAPE. One row per draft, carrying its revision history INSIDE the row.
/// Compare the two neighbours built from the SAME two events, because "what is one row" is the whole
/// question and it has three defensible answers:
///
///   MyDrafts      one row per draft, FLATTENED — only the current state. No history at all.
///   DraftHistory  one row per draft, with the history as a repeated group inside it.  (this file)
///   DeliveryLog   one row per CHILD, in state-view/ — an EventProjection, one document per event.
///
