    /// uncached that is invisible; the moment a second-level aggregate cache holds that instance
    /// (<c>Options.CacheLimitPerTenant</c> on the projection, or <c>UseIdentityMapForAggregates</c> on
    /// the store) the mutation escapes the transaction that made it, and a rolled-back or re-run batch
    /// leaves a row with duplicated members. On an array <c>.Add</c> does not exist, so the immutable
    /// <c>with { … = [.. …, item] }</c> below is the only way through and the bug cannot be written.
    ///
